{"authored" [{"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad36ea6479b1a7965667df614cf6bd2e83acc0bb6fd960e9a47cceafeaae72f7" "basis" 1515 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad36ea6479b1a7965667df614cf6bd2e83acc0bb6fd960e9a47cceafeaae72f7" "basis" 1515 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "419bff3195711dba4c75f08f3c1717b4688a5cc9704c9527092dd16761cd9b19" "basis" 1515 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad36ea6479b1a7965667df614cf6bd2e83acc0bb6fd960e9a47cceafeaae72f7" "basis" 1515 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/state.json" "file_sha256" "ad36ea6479b1a7965667df614cf6bd2e83acc0bb6fd960e9a47cceafeaae72f7" "basis" 1515 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041466/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2y}} \\\\ {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{2y} & =2{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+C) & =0 \\\\ 2+C & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6cd6ea9028bcde8009f6010933e7dd4de81e8a086f50ec223aba3e414f32cc2"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4{e}^{x}-3)"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-{e}^{x})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{e}^{x}+1}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-4016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-14310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1$ given that  $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-14310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ to find $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C) \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ C & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-14310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6cd6ea9028bcde8009f6010933e7dd4de81e8a086f50ec223aba3e414f32cc2"} {"question" "q-14310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-14310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-14310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${sec}^{2}⁡(4y){y}^{′}={sec}^{2}⁡(7x)$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{8}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡(7x) \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={sec}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=4{C}_{1}.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(4\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7\\cdot 0)+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355544" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6cd6ea9028bcde8009f6010933e7dd4de81e8a086f50ec223aba3e414f32cc2"} {"question" "q-355544" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355544" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{7}\\tan(7x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(1)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6cd6ea9028bcde8009f6010933e7dd4de81e8a086f50ec223aba3e414f32cc2"} {"question" "q-355546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4x^2-\\frac{5}{x}+7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6cd6ea9028bcde8009f6010933e7dd4de81e8a086f50ec223aba3e414f32cc2"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14057251/state.json" "file_sha256" "62d8be4d91dfb53102eb83a45fd440f7715e16c2571251e7e260b54dd476bb1c"}] "usage" {"q-355577" []} "basis" 1860 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186290366] "immutable_fields" [[17592186290365 :answer-field/correct] [17592186290365 :answer-field/id] [